use /std/{Bytes, Io};
use /std/Bool/{Holds};

--- One read's answer: bytes, the end of the stream, or a failure.
---
--- A chunk holds at least one byte, and says so: a read asks for a positive count, and a stream with nothing more to give has ended, which is `eof`. So a reader takes a chunk's first byte by its proof rather than by a default, and a loop over chunks advances with every one.
pub induct Chunk: pub Type
--- Bytes were read: at least one.
| chunk(bytes: Bytes, @some: Holds(0 < Bytes/len(bytes)))
--- The stream is finished.
| eof()
--- The read failed.
| error(Io/Error)
end

pub use Chunk/*;
